      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The erratic jitter without physical signal degradation suggests it might be related to MAC layer or higher layer protocols. Common culprits include non-union 802.1Q VLANs, double stacking, incorrect port-based traffic shaping, or packet loss from upstream routers that is not being dropped locally. Additionally, queueing behavior or high CPU utilization on the edge router could also contribute to the erratic jitter patterns you're seeing.",
      "source": "target",
